(PROJECT RESCUE - ROUND 1 PROPOSAL \(REVIEW DRAFT\)) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. What does your Skill do? \(one sentence\)) Tj T*
(   Project Rescue finds a context-supported candidate for a missing project file and) Tj T*
(   proposes one approved copy that preserves the source.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(2. Who is your target user, and what is their problem?) Tj T*
(   Creators and small teams may have a missing project dependency while an existing) Tj T*
(   usable copy has an opaque name, outdated alternatives, or another active use.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(3. What is your solution?) Tj T*
(   Compare the missing reference, review history and candidate records to identify a) Tj T*
(   supported version; explain contradictions and stop when identity is ambiguous.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(4. What is the main user flow?) Tj T*
(   Authorize folders, investigate references and candidates, review one proposed) Tj T*
(   source and destination, approve the exact operation, and independently verify the) Tj T*
(   copy if the platform can safely execute it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(5. How is your idea different from existing tools or common AI solutions?) Tj T*
(   The intended workflow combines cross-file identity evidence, shared-source) Tj T*
(   preservation and approval-gated action across project types. Generic AI and) Tj T*
(   application-specific relinking overlap; superior performance and uniqueness are not) Tj T*
(   established.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(6. Which UGREEN AI NAS features does your Skill use, and at which step?) Tj T*
(   File-agent discovers, reads, checks paths and hashes, and conditionally copies;) Tj T*
(   document-agent extracts and compares project references. All work stays within) Tj T*
(   owner-authorized scopes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(7. What is your technical approach?) Tj T*
(   A Markdown parent delegates to registered experts using actual completed results.) Tj T*
(   The user supplies the goal and source and destination authorization. Separate owner) Tj T*
(   and gateway approval are required; uncertain identity, collisions or unestablished) Tj T*
(   atomic no-overwrite stop execution. Runtime model and data flows depend on UGREEN) Tj T*
(   configuration.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(8. What have you built so far? What is not built yet? What still needs testing on a) Tj T*
(NAS?) Tj T*
(   A Markdown Skill passed static checking. Local Codex identified intended candidates) Tj T*
(   in two fictional archives; generic Codex did too. A separate local adapter copied) Tj T*
(   one file with simulated approvals. Real NAS execution, safe copy semantics,) Tj T*
(   approval resumption and readback remain untested.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
ET
